course: dictionary
lesson: 11254
title: Worth: value, effort and importance
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Worth has a few jobs, and each one is about value. The first is money: «a dime is worth 10 cents» tells you what the coin is worth, which is 10 cents. Ask yourself: is this about money, or about whether something is good enough?
explain: After words like «is» or «it's», worth often means good enough to spend time, money or effort on. «Is it worth it?» asks if something is good enough to bother with. «It's worth learning how a place uses the clock before judging it» means learning about it is useful and well spent time.
explain: You can also say «10 dollars' worth of» something, which means as much as 10 dollars buys. To check any meaning, swap in your own words. «Spices were not usually as valuable as gold» still makes sense, so worth means value here.
fact: Worth can be a noun or an adjective, so it can be used in more than one way.
fact: «Worth» can mean the money something could be sold for: «a dime is worth 10 cents».
fact: «Worth it» or «worth doing» means good enough to spend your time, money or effort on.
fact: A person's worth is how valuable or important they are.
fact: The Rat says there is «nothing half so much worth doing as simply messing about in boats»: he means he loves it most, and it is a loving exaggeration.
exercise: «A dime is worth 10 cents.» What does worth tell us? | It is a very shiny coin | It is a kind of sweet | It weighs 10 grams | *How much money it could be sold for
exercise: Mia asks, «Is it worth it?» What does she want to know? | Whether it is very old | Whether it is made of gold | Whether it is for a dog | *Whether it is good enough to spend time, money or effort on
exercise: Each sticker is worth 5 pence. How much are 4 stickers worth? | 1 pence | *20 pence | 9 pence | 54 pence
test: «It's worth learning how a place uses the clock before judging it.» What does worth mean here? | Worth money in a shop | Made of wood | *Good enough to spend time on | Weighs a lot
test: What does «10 dollars' worth of» mean? | A dollar and a dime | Exactly 10 sweets | The price of one shop | *As much as 10 dollars buys
exam: What does a person's worth mean? | *How valuable or important they are | How many friends they have | How tall they are | How much they can carry
